@startuml
' US-16 — Organise the library, and set the reader's preferences.
' Communication — the objects that take part, and what each one is asked
' Sources: ../../../analysis/stories.md (US-16), ../../../specification/03-features.md (F-23, F-27)
'
' A sequence would answer "in what order". This one answers "between whom":
' the page asks, the reader decides, the disk holds, and the browser's storage
' keeps the choices.

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor White
  BorderColor #333
  ArrowColor #333
}

[Library page] as LIB
[Settings panel] as SET
[Reader\n(server.py)] as SRV
[Files\n(kinds, roots, writes)] as FILES
[The disk] as DISK
[Storage\n(localStorage)] as STORE

LIB --> SRV : GET /library
SRV --> FILES : the kinds of a folder
FILES --> DISK : the names
SRV --> LIB : the folders, the notes, the kinds

Reader -> LIB : picks a change
LIB --> SRV : POST /api/rename, /api/delete,\n/api/mkdir, /api/upload
SRV --> FILES : the change
FILES --> DISK : the change is made (D5)
DISK --> SRV : the answer
SRV --> LIB : the answer, or the reason

Reader -> SET : picks a choice
SET --> STORE : the choice, under the reader's key (F-27)
STORE --> SET : the choices, when the page opens

note bottom of FILES
  F-23: the library keeps notes, pictures and
  spreadsheets. The refusal names the kinds
  it keeps.

  D5: the reader is the only writer. Nothing
  else writes to the disk.
end note

note bottom of STORE
  S-6: the state lives in the browser's storage
  and nowhere else. The reader keeps nothing
  about the person who reads.
end note
@enduml
